,7:headers;1620:40:4:Date,29:Mon, 06 Apr 2026 14:03:17 GMT,]52:12:Content-Type,32:text/event-stream; charset=utf-8,]31:17:Transfer-Encoding,7:chunked,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:13:Cache-Control,8:no-cache,]52:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-limit,7:2000000,]56:42:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-remaining,7:1989000,]66:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:03:12Z,]52:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-limit,6:400000,]56:43:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-remaining,6:400000,]67:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:03:11Z,]45:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-limit,4:4000,]49:38:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-remaining,4:3999,]62:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:03:11Z,]46:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-limit,7:2400000,]50:36:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining,7:2389000,]60:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T14:03:11Z,]46:10:request-id,28:req_011CZneCUwMHZQj9XKvBLxU6,]77:25:strict-transport-security,44:max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload,]69:25:anthropic-organization-id,36:19d39eaa-efb4-49e0-afe8-a7359703719a,]23:6:Server,10:cloudflare,]40:29:x-envoy-upstream-service-time,4:5314,]46:13:server-timing,25:x-originResponse;dur=5316,]29:15:cf-cache-status,7:DYNAMIC,]208:10:set-cookie,189:_cfuvid=ba70FFFnrlGNuZCYG1kJsEPNcCnfMWMAnonnVCI6j40-1775484191.8193998-1.0.1.1-fPgjHOVZtxD1uMUVGt7p78DXmRIsQLyldcu1NRdK9Eo; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e8155a6db1fbe01-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;61707:4:path;12:/v1/messages,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;18:1775484191.7078846^15:timestamp_start;18:1775484191.7071824^8:trailers;0:~7:content;60919:{"max_tokens":32768,"messages":[{"content":[{"text":"---\n## üîç Entering Phase: Explore\nYou are now in the **Explore** phase. Set aside any goals, plans, or assumptions from previous phases ‚Äî they no longer apply. Your only objective is defined below.\n---\n\nYou are a file search specialist for Claude Code, Anthropic's official CLI for Claude. You excel at thoroughly navigating and exploring codebases.\n\n=== CRITICAL: READ-ONLY MODE - NO FILE MODIFICATIONS ===\nThis is a READ-ONLY exploration task. You are STRICTLY PROHIBITED from:\n- Creating new files (no Write, touch, or file creation of any kind)\n- Modifying existing files (no Edit operations)\n- Deleting files (no rm or deletion)\n- Moving or copying files (no mv or cp)\n- Creating temporary files anywhere, including /tmp\n- Using redirect operators (\u003e, \u003e\u003e, |) or heredocs to write to files\n- Running ANY commands that change system state\n\nYour role is EXCLUSIVELY to search and analyze existing code. You do NOT have access to file editing tools - attempting to edit files will fail.\n\nYour strengths:\n- Rapidly finding files using glob patterns\n- Searching code and text with powerful regex patterns\n- Reading and analyzing file contents\n\nGuidelines:\n- Use Glob for broad file pattern matching\n- Use Grep for searching file contents with regex\n- Use Read when you know the specific file path you need to read ‚Äî files are always returned in minified form (whitespace collapsed, comments stripped)\n- Use Bash ONLY for read-only operations (ls, git status, git log, git diff, find, cat, head, tail)\n- NEVER use Bash for: mkdir, touch, rm, cp, mv, git add, git commit, npm install, pip install, or any file creation/modification\n- Adapt your search approach based on the thoroughness level specified by the caller\n- Return file paths as absolute paths in your final response\n- For clear communication, avoid using emojis\n\nNOTE: You are meant to be a fast agent that returns output as quickly as possible. In order to achieve this you must:\n- Make efficient use of the tools that you have at your disposal: be smart about how you search for files and implementations\n- Wherever possible you should try to spawn multiple parallel tool calls for grepping and reading files\n\nComplete the user's search request efficiently.\n\nNotes:\n- Agent threads always have their cwd reset between bash calls, as a result please only use absolute file paths.\n- Any file paths you return in your response MUST be absolute. Do NOT use relative paths.\n- For clear communication with the user the assistant MUST avoid using emojis.\n- Do not use a colon before tool calls. Text like \"Let me read the file:\" followed by a read tool call should just be \"Let me read the file.\" with a period.\n\nHere is useful information about the environment you are running in:\n\u003cenv\u003e\nWorking directory: /workspace\nIs directory a git repo: Yes\nPlatform: linux\nShell: sh\nOS Version: 6.10.14-linuxkit\n\u003c/env\u003e\nYou are powered by the model claude-sonnet-4-6.\n\n# Goal\n\nYour goal is to explore this codebase as grounding for planning and implementation. Say \"Exploration done\" when you are done, do not summarize your findings.\n\nHere is the user request:\n\u003c/user_request\u003e\nAdd French language support, as requested in issue #3460. Explore the codebase to find how existing languages and localization are handled, then add complete French (fr) translations following the same patterns. Make sure any existing tests still pass after your changes. Create a PR-ready branch with your work.\ncf. https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/3460\n\u003c/user_request\u003e","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"text":"I'll explore the codebase to understand how localization and language support is currently implemented.","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_011cXrwS6ihnw6X9AbKJqV1u","input":{"pattern":["**/*"],"path":["/workspace"],"reason":"Get an overview of the entire project structure to understand what kind of project this is and how it's organized.","type":"d"},"name":"glob_files","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_01FDfvahK5Pr7R9smYrNoVSk","input":{"command":"ls /workspace","reason":"Get top-level directory listing to understand project structure.","reason_to_use_instead_of_read_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_edit_file_tool":"N/A","reason_to_use_instead_of_glob_files_tool":"Need to see actual directory listing with ordering"},"name":"bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011cXrwS6ihnw6X9AbKJqV1u","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"/workspace/.agent\n/workspace/.agent/workflows\n/workspace/.agents\n/workspace/.agents/skills\n/workspace/.agents/skills/parallels-discord-roundtrip\n/workspace/.git\n/workspace/.git/branches\n/workspace/.git/hooks\n/workspace/.git/info\n/workspace/.git/logs\n/workspace/.git/logs/refs\n/workspace/.git/logs/refs/heads\n/workspace/.git/logs/refs/remotes\n/workspace/.git/logs/refs/remotes/origin\n/workspace/.git/objects\n/workspace/.git/objects/info\n/workspace/.git/objects/pack\n/workspace/.git/refs\n/workspace/.git/refs/heads\n/workspace/.git/refs/remotes\n/workspace/.git/refs/remotes/origin\n/workspace/.git/refs/tags\n/workspace/.github\n/workspace/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE\n/workspace/.github/actions\n/workspace/.github/actions/detect-docs-changes\n/workspace/.github/actions/ensure-base-commit\n/workspace/.github/actions/setup-node-env\n/workspace/.github/actions/setup-pnpm-store-cache\n/workspace/.github/codeql\n/workspace/.github/instructions\n/workspace/.github/workflows\n/workspace/.pi\n/workspace/.pi/extensions\n/workspace/.pi/extensions/ui\n/workspace/.pi/git\n/workspace/.pi/prompts\n/workspace/.vix\n/workspace/.vscode\n/workspace/Swabble\n/workspace/Swabble/.github\n/workspace/Swabble/.github/workflows\n/workspace/Swabble/Sources\n/workspace/Swabble/Sources/SwabbleCore\n/workspace/Swabble/Sources/SwabbleCore/Config\n/workspace/Swabble/Sources/SwabbleCore/Hooks\n/workspace/Swabble/Sources/SwabbleCore/Speech\n/workspace/Swabble/Sources/SwabbleCore/Su